From d350c077c90910e6dea5a8bfd697ad5c26d23720 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GrgaPalcic <26028466+GrgaPalcic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:30:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: a failed disk recall under TF_KV_SHARE costs a cold
 pass, not the lane

Rank 0 gives the pages back, drops the blank state, marks the disk state unreadable for this process and counts disk_recalls_failed. A rank other than 0 no longer leaves its step loop on a failed disk op: it poisons the state being recalled, skips that state's later writes and answers the seal and each read with a status word. A failed read for a save leaves the kept state in place.
---
